%E7%93%9C&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.cup.com.hk%2F2016%2F10%2F31%2Ffrom-turnip-to-pumpkin-the-jack-o-lantern%2F&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Martin&#95;2022&#95;z365-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Martin_2022_z365_2-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMartin2022\" class=\"citation web\">Martin, Emily. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/the-history-of-trick-or-treating-and-how-it-became-a-halloween-tradition\">The history of trick-or-treating, and how it became a Halloween tradition</a>. Culture. 2022-10-24 <span class=\"reference-accessdate\"> &#91;<span class=\"nowrap\">2024-01-17</span>&#93;</span>. （原始內容<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20230606085810/https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/the-history-of-trick-or-treating-and-how-it-became-a-halloween-tradition\">存檔</a>於2023-06-06）.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.atitle=The+history+of+trick-or-treating%2C+and+how+it+became+a+Halloween+tradition&amp;rft.aufirst=Emily&amp;rft.aulast=Martin&amp;rft.date=2022-10-24&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Culture&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nationalgeographic.com%2Fculture%2Farticle%2Fthe-history-of-trick-or-treating-and-how-it-became-a-halloween-tradition&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-guising&#95;definition-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-guising_definition_3-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite class=\"citation web\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20210717193112/https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/guising\">Definition of \"guising<span style=\"padding-right:0.2em;\">\"</span></a>. <i>Collins English Dictionary</i>.  <span class=\"reference-accessdate\"> &#91;<span class=\"nowrap\">2019-03-03</span>&#93;</span>. （<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.collinsdictionary.com/dictionary/english/guising\">原始內容</a>存檔於2021-07-17）. <q>(in Scotland and N England) the practice or custom of disguising oneself in fancy dress, often with a mask, and visiting people's houses, esp at Halloween</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.btitle=Definition+of+%22guising%22&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.pub=%27%27Collins+English+Dictionary%27%27&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.collinsdictionary.com%2Fdictionary%2Fenglish%2Fguising&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Magazine&#95;Sonja&#95;Anderson&#95;2023&#95;k845-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Magazine_Sonja_Anderson_2023_k845_4-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMagazineSonja&#95;Anderson2023\" class=\"citation web\">Magazine, Smithsonian; Sonja Anderson, Rose Eveleth. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-history-of-trick-or-treating-goes-back-centuries-79408373/\">The History of Trick-or-Treating Goes Back Centuries</a>. Smithsonian Magazine. 2023-10-24 <span class=\"reference-accessdate\"> &#91;<span class=\"nowrap\">2024-01-17</span>&#93;</span>. （原始內容<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240508211309/https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-history-of-trick-or-treating-goes-back-centuries-79408373/\">存檔</a>於2024-05-08）.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.atitle=The+History+of+Trick-or-Treating+Goes+Back+Centuries&amp;rft.au=Sonja+Anderson%2C+Rose+Eveleth&amp;rft.aufirst=Smithsonian&amp;rft.aulast=Magazine&amp;rft.date=2023-10-24&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Smithsonian+Magazine&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.smithsonianmag.com%2Fsmart-news%2Fthe-history-of-trick-or-treating-goes-back-centuries-79408373%2F&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Peddle, S. V. (2007). <i>Pagan Channel Islands: Europe's Hidden Heritage</i>. p.54</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-6\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-6\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i>British Folk Customs</i>, Christina Hole (1976), p.91</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Jackson1995-7\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Jackson1995_7-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFJackson1995\" class=\"citation book\">Jackson, Jeanne L. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/redletterdays0000jean\">Red Letter Days: The Christian Year in Story for Primary Assembly</a>. <a href=\"/w/index.php?title=Nelson_Thornes&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Nelson Thornes（頁面不存在）\">Nelson Thornes</a>. 1 January 1995: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/redletterdays0000jean/page/158\">158</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/9780748719341\" title=\"Special:BookSources/9780748719341\"><span title=\"國際標準書號\">ISBN</span>&#160;9780748719341</a>. <q>Later, it became the custom for poorer Christians to offer prayers for the dead, in return for money or food (soul cakes) from their wealthier neighbours. People would go 'souling' - rather like carol singing - requesting alms or soul cakes: 'A soul, a soul, a soul cake, Please to give us a soul cake, One for Peter, two for Paul, have mercy on us Christians all.'</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.aufirst=Jeanne+L.&amp;rft.aulast=Jackson&amp;rft.btitle=Red+Letter+Days%3A+The+Christian+Year+in+Story+for+Primary+Assembly&amp;rft.date=1995-01-01&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.isbn=9780748719341&amp;rft.pages=158&amp;rft.pub=Nelson+Thornes&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Fredletterdays0000jean&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-hutton374-375-8\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-hutton374-375_8-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Hutton, pp.374–375</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-9\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-9\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Cleene, Marcel. <i>Compendium of Symbolic and Ritual Plants in Europe</i>. Man &amp; Culture, 2002. p.108. Quote: \"Soul cakes were small cakes baked as food for the deceased or offered for the salvation of their souls. They were therefore offered at funerals and feasts of the dead, laid on graves, or given to the poor as representatives of the dead. The baking of these soul cakes is a universal practice\".</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Dodge1883-10\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Dodge1883_10-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMary&#95;Mapes&#95;Dodge1883\" class=\"citation book\"><a href=\"/w/index.php?title=Mary_Mapes_Dodge&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mary Mapes Dodge（頁面不存在）\">Mary Mapes Dodge</a> (編). <a href=\"/w/index.php?title=St._Nicholas_Magazine&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"St. Nicholas Magazine（页面不存在）\">St. Nicholas Magazine</a>. Scribner &amp; Company. 1883: 93. <q>Soul-cakes,\" which the rich gave to the poor at the Halloween season, in return for which the recipients prayed for the souls of the givers and their friends. And this custom became so favored in popular esteem that, for a long time, it was a regular observance in the country towns of England for small companies to go from parish to parish at Halloween, begging soul-cakes by singing under the windows some such verse as this: \"Soul, souls, for a soul-cake; Pray you good mistress, a soul-cake!\"</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.au=Mary+Mapes+Dodge&amp;rft.btitle=St.+Nicholas+Magazine&amp;rft.date=1883&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.pages=93&amp;rft.pub=Scribner+%26+Company&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook\" class=\"Z3988\"><span style=\"display:none;\">&#160;</span></span> <span style=\"display:none;font-size:100%\" class=\"error citation-comment\">使用<code style=\"color:inherit; border:inherit; padding:inherit;\">&#124;accessdate=</code>需要含有<code style=\"color:inherit; border:inherit; padding:inherit;\">&#124;url=</code> (<a href=\"/wiki/Help:%E5%BC%95%E6%96%87%E6%A0%BC%E5%BC%8F1%E9%94%99%E8%AF%AF#accessdate_missing_url\" title=\"Help:引文格式1錯誤\">幫助</a>)</span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-miles-11\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-miles_11-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Miles, Clement A. (1912). <i>Christmas in Ritual and Tradition</i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.sacred-texts.com/time/crt/crt11.htm\">Chapter 7: All Hallow Tide to Martinmas</a> （<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//web.archive.org/web/20131104130353/http://www.sacred-texts.com/time/crt/crt11.htm\">頁面存檔備份</a>，存於<a href=\"/wiki/%E4%BA%92%E8%81%94%E7%BD%91%E6%A1%A3%E6%A1%88%E9%A6%86\" title=\"網際網路檔案館\">網際網路檔案館</a>）.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-mcneill2-12\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-mcneill2_12-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">McNeill, F. Marian. <i>Hallowe'en: its origin, rites and ceremonies in the Scottish tradition</i>. Albyn Press, 1970. pp.29–31</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-13\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-13\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><i>Journal of the Royal Society of Antiquaries of Ireland, Volume 2</i>. 1855. pp.308-309</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-Guising-14\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-Guising_14-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Rogers, Nicholas. (2002) \"Coming Over: Halloween in North America\". <i>Halloween: From Pagan Ritual to Party Night</i>. p.76. Oxford University Press, 2002, <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><a href=\"/wiki/%E5%9B%BD%E9%99%85%E6%A0%87%E5%87%86%E4%B9%A6%E5%8F%B7\" title=\"國際標準書號\">ISBN</a>&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-19-514691-3\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-19-514691-3\">0-19-514691-3</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-15\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-15\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">\"'Trick or Treat' Is Demand,\" <i>Herald</i> (<a href=\"/wiki/Lethbridge\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lethbridge\">Lethbridge</a>, Alberta), November 4, 1927, p. 5, dateline <a href=\"/w/index.php?title=Blackie,_Alberta&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Blackie, Alberta（頁面不存在）\">Blackie, Alberta</a>, Canada Nov. 3.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-16\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-16\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Moss, Doris Hudson. \"A Victim of the Window-Soaping Brigade?\" <i>The American Home</i>, November 1939, p. 48. Moss was a California-based writer.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-17\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-17\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r95173179\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFMorton2012\" class=\"citation book\">Morton, Lisa. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/trickortreathist0000mort\">Trick or Treat a history of halloween</a>. Reaktion Books. 2012: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://archive.org/details/trickortreathist0000mort/page/64\">64</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/9781780231877\" title=\"Special:BookSources/9781780231877\"><span title=\"國際標準書號\">ISBN</span>&#160;9781780231877</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fzh.wikipedia.org%3A%E4%B8%8D%E7%B5%A6%E7%B3%96%E5%B0%B1%E6%90%97%E8%9B%8B&amp;rft.aufirst=Lisa&amp;rft.aulast=Morton&amp;rft.btitle=Trick+or+Treat+a+history+of+halloween&amp;rft.date=2012&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.isbn=9781780231877&amp;rft.pages=64&amp;rft.pub=Reaktion+Books&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.org%2Fdetails%2Ftrickortreathist0000mort&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook\" class=\"Z3988\"><span st